@doc """
Renders a styled cluster.

Generated by `mix flint.add cluster`. Theming lives in `flint.css`; this wrapper
maps `align`, `gap`, and `justify` onto the matching `data-*` hooks the theme
targets. The defaults are `align="center"`, `gap="md"`, and `justify="start"`.
Children wrap onto new lines as space runs out; `justify="split"` keeps the last
child at the inline end after the row wraps. `as` is forwarded to the headless
component, and `as="ul"` or `as="ol"` resets the list chrome while keeping the
native list semantics. Headless structure comes from `FlintUI.cluster`.
"""
<%= @attrs %>
<%= @slots %>

def <%= @name %>(assigns) do
  ~H"""
  <FlintUI.cluster
    data-cluster
    data-align={@align}
    data-gap={@gap}
    data-justify={@justify}
    class={@class}
    {@rest}
  >
    {render_slot(@inner_block)}
  </FlintUI.cluster>
  """
end
